{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"criteria":[{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":84,"line_start":80,"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py"},"criterion":"The janitor gains a count-denominated axis (`max_entries`) that engages independently of disk headroom, so a host with abundant free space still bounds the store. Default `DEFAULT_MAX_ENTRIES = 2000`, ON by default (`0` is the operator opt-out).","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":912,"line_start":886,"path":"tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py"},"criterion":"A test reclaims on a store under EVERY pre-existing threshold at once: `free_bytes=10**15`, `max_bytes=0`, `free_watermark_pct=0`, `max_age_seconds=10**9`.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":500,"line_start":425,"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py"},"criterion":"The axis composes with the existing hysteresis (target `max_entries * 95 // 100`) rather than re-firing every pass, and respects `grace_seconds` so an entry in use by a concurrent gate is never evicted — obtained by joining `over_count` into `wants_room` rather than adding a parallel path.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":1002,"line_start":995,"path":"tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py"},"criterion":"Enforcement rides the existing operation-linked trigger: no new daemon, no CI dependency (`project.portability`), and `maybe_gc`'s decision remains one `stat` of the stamp sidecar — the store is never enumerated to decide whether to run. Verified by `gc_trigger.py` carrying a docstring change only.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":217,"line_start":217,"path":"src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py"},"criterion":"Tunable via `REBAR_GATE_MAX_ENTRIES` env > `[snapshot] max_entries` > default, through the existing config seam.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":613,"line_start":574,"path":"docs/config.md"},"criterion":"An operator note documents the default, tuning in both directions, and a one-off foreground reclaim for already-bloated hosts that still honours `grace_seconds`.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":441,"line_start":425,"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py"},"criterion":"Bug 'Unbounded gate-snapshot accumulation in TMPDIR drives fseventsd to 26GB RSS and starves the host' is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_fingerprint":null,"metrics":{"alias_index_build_ms":891,"commits_inspected":2789,"descendant_ids":0,"descendant_scope_ms":2660,"det_ms":9225.9,"diff_validation_ms":109,"distinct_references":2327,"git_history_read_ms":189,"landing_check_ms":1247,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":88674.3,"material_policy_ms":0,"pre_verifier_total_ms":9306,"referencing_commits_found":1,"requests":14,"structural_scan_ms":4979,"ticket_ref_resolution_ms":26,"tool_calls":14,"total_ms":97948.3,"verifier_annotation_ms":0,"verifier_attempt_count":1,"verifier_attempt_setup_ms":2,"verifier_attempts_ms":269591,"verifier_between_attempts_ms":0,"verifier_build_drift_ms":530,"verifier_call_ms":269614,"verifier_code_snapshot_ms":3086,"verifier_completion_agent_ms":88674,"verifier_dispatch_finalization_ms":0,"verifier_dispatch_ms":99743,"verifier_dispatch_setup_ms":1795,"verifier_handle_apply_ms":0,"verifier_handle_defaults_ms":0,"verifier_handle_resolution_ms":158819,"verifier_inner_setup_ms":11025,"verifier_no_llm_passthrough_ms":0,"verifier_precheck_context_ms":9209,"verifier_resume_config_ms":0,"verifier_resume_count":0,"verifier_reusable_lookup_m